-- title:
--   Longitudinal and transverse rank factors
-- statement:
--   Choose a distinguished coordinate $i$, longitudinal scale $L$, transverse scale $M$, and a positive packing parameter $P$. The lower and upper side parameters are
--
--   $$ \delta_j=\frac{L\mathbf1_{j=i}+M\mathbf1_{j\ne i}}{32P},\qquad U_j=6\bigl(L\mathbf1_{j=i}+M\mathbf1_{j\ne i}\bigr). $$
--
--   Recursive nonnegative factors record longitudinal growth independently of the joint contraction constant, while transverse factors may depend on that constant. The separation of these dependencies is needed for successive scale choice.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Continuous graph homomorphisms of higher dimensional abelian group actions, arXiv:2609.39824v1 (2026), Section(s) 5–6; https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.39824v1. This item is auxiliary infrastructure of the accompanying formalization, not a claim that each implementation definition is separately numbered in the paper. Original Lean module AbelianTargets/AnisotropicRankRates.lean, selected declaration lines 10-11, 13-14, 16-18, 20-24; SHA-256 804090b6616c6aaf97aa2f4286c987e3d71c4e28833691258bb43b18f4bf0b3a. Selected spans are from the final generated manifest. The original source snapshot is local; no public repository URL or commit was available.

